# Jira ticket ↔ pull request mapping

> Cursor mirror of the canonical user-level rule `~/.claude/rules/jira-ticket-pr-mapping.md`.
> Edit the canonical file first, then this mirror.

A PROD automation moves a ticket to BA Acceptance when a pull request whose branch
or title contains its key is **merged into a trunk** — `staging`, `www-new-release`, or `dev`
(pakfactory.com-server) — unless
the ticket is already in BA Acceptance. So **merging a keyed PR into a trunk is
a forward transition** — it summons a reviewer — and falls under
`jira-transition-gate.md`. Opening a PR is free: open early, review on the PR.
Promotion merges into `main` do not trigger it.

Applies to every repo whose branches or PR titles carry a PROD key.

## Rules

1. **A ticket without subtasks ships as one PR per repo.** Fixes found while
   reviewing go on the same PR before merge — no follow-up PRs against an
   unmerged ticket.
2. **Split into subtasks up front when** the work has phases/milestones, spans
   repos that merge or deploy at different times, or would not be reviewable in
   one sitting (~600 changed lines, excluding generated/lock files). Each subtask
   has its own key, one PR, and its own acceptance criteria. Subtasks reach BA
   Acceptance too — each subtask merge summons the reviewer, by design.
3. **Cross-repo work landing together** (both PRs merged in the same session)
   stays one ticket.
4. **Subtask PRs never stack.** Base each on its repo's trunk (`staging`,
   `www-new-release` for the www rebuild, `dev` for pakfactory.com-server) after its predecessor merges.
5. **Follow-ups after merge:**
   - Ticket still in BA Acceptance → same ticket, new PR; its merge does not
     move or re-notify (the automation skips tickets already there).
   - Ticket bounced back by the reviewer → same ticket, new PR; its merge returns
     it to BA Acceptance, which is the intended hand-back.
   - Ticket Done → new bug ticket linked to the original. Do not reopen.
6. **An agent never merges a keyed PR** without the `jira-transition-gate.md`
   confirmation block and an explicit yes.
7. **PRs that carry several keys** (e.g. the `www-new-release` → `staging` launch
   PR) move every keyed ticket on merge. Keep keys out of their titles, or confirm
   each ticket before merging — one confirmation per ticket, never a batch.

## Why

PROD-2628: 7 pakfactory.com-server PRs + 1 pakfactory.com PR each moved the
ticket to BA Acceptance on open and were reverted by hand; every early PR
summoned a reviewer to unfinished work. On 2026-10-01 the trigger was switched
from PR opened to PR merged (into `staging`, `www-new-release` or `dev`) with the
condition status ≠ BA Acceptance.

